.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KCLONE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kclone
.Nd copy a ZFS dataset instantly, as a clone mounted somewhere else
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar source-path
.Ar dest-path
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
snapshots the dataset mounted at
.Ar source-path
and clones the snapshot as a new dataset mounted at
.Ar dest-path .
The clone shares every block with the snapshot: it takes no time and no
space until one of the two is changed.
It is a way to try something on a copy of a database directory, a home
or a site, and throw the copy away.
.Pp
The new dataset is named after
.Ar dest-path
under the source's pool:
.Pa /srv/web-test
becomes
.Ql rpool/srv/web-test .
.Pp
It refuses, before changing anything:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
a source that is not a ZFS dataset's mountpoint \(em a directory inside a
dataset, since the whole dataset is what would be cloned, or a path on
another filesystem;
.It
a destination dataset that exists, or whose parent does not;
.It
a destination directory with files in it, which the clone would hide;
.It
a destination that is not an absolute path of plain characters.
.El
If the clone fails, the snapshot taken for it is removed.
.Pp
.Nm
calls
.Xr zfs 8
through
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Cloned.
.It 1
Refused, or the clone failed.
.It 2
Not two arguments.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, from a throwaway dataset,
.Ql rpool/kct-3554540
mounted at
.Pa /var/tmp/kct-3554540 ,
holding
.Pa data.txt ;
all removed afterwards.
.Ss A clone
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kclone /var/tmp/kct-3554540 /srv/kct-3554540-copy
[kclone] Source:      rpool/kct-3554540 (/var/tmp/kct-3554540)
[kclone] Destination: rpool/srv/kct-3554540-copy (/srv/kct-3554540-copy)
[kclone] Creating snapshot: rpool/kct-3554540@clone-20260930-000548
[kclone] Cloning (CoW — near-instant, near-zero space)...
[kclone] Done.
[kclone]
[kclone]   Source:  /var/tmp/kct-3554540 → rpool/kct-3554540
[kclone]   Clone:   /srv/kct-3554540-copy → rpool/srv/kct-3554540-copy
[kclone]   Size:    0B (CoW — grows only as changes are made)
[kclone]
[kclone]   To destroy:  sudo zfs destroy rpool/srv/kct-3554540-copy && sudo zfs destroy rpool/kct-3554540@clone-20260930-000548
# (exited 0)
$ cat /srv/kct-3554540-copy/data.txt
original
.Ed
.Ss What it refuses
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kclone /var/tmp/kct-3554540/sub /srv/kct-3554540-sub
[kclone] /var/tmp/kct-3554540/sub is inside rpool/kct-3554540 (mounted at /var/tmp/kct-3554540), not a dataset of its own; kclone copies a whole dataset -- give /var/tmp/kct-3554540
# (exited 1)
$ kclone /dev/shm /srv/kct-3554540-shm
[kclone] /dev/shm is not on a ZFS dataset
# (exited 1)
$ kclone /var/tmp/kct-3554540 /srv/kct-3554540-copy
[kclone] Destination already exists: rpool/srv/kct-3554540-copy (/srv/kct-3554540-copy)
# (exited 1)
$ kclone /var/tmp/kct-3554540 /nonexistent-3554540/x
[kclone] no dataset rpool/nonexistent-3554540 to put rpool/nonexistent-3554540/x under; create it first (zfs create -p)
# (exited 1)
$ kclone /var/tmp/kct-3554540 /srv/kct-3554540-full
[kclone] /srv/kct-3554540-full is a directory with files in it; the clone would hide them
# (exited 1)
$ kclone /var/tmp/kct-3554540 "/srv/a b"
[kclone] '/srv/a b' must be an absolute path of plain characters, without .. or a trailing /
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kdf 8 ,
.Xr ksnap 8 ,
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr zfs-clone 8 ,
.Xr zfs-promote 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: a directory inside a dataset was taken
for the dataset, so asking to copy one directory of a home cloned the
whole home; a path on another filesystem was taken for a dataset named
after it; a destination directory with files in it was mounted over; and
a destination whose parent dataset did not exist failed only after the
snapshot was taken, and left it.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The source's snapshot, and so the source, cannot be destroyed while the
clone exists.
To keep the clone and let the source go, promote it with
.Xr zfs-promote 8 .
.Pp
To remove the clone, destroy it and then its snapshot, as the last line
of the output says.
